ponema pallidum</italic> evolution: Toward clarity?</article-title><source>PLoS Negl Trop Dis</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>e184</fpage><comment>doi:10.1371/journal.pntd.0000184</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18357339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-World1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Yaws: A forgotten disease.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/neglected_diseases/diseases/yaws/en/index.html">http://www.who.int/neglected_diseases/diseases/yaws/en/index.html</ext-link>. Accessed 1 August 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Ohenjo1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ohenjo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Nettleton</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Good</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Indigenous health 3. Health of indigenous people in Africa.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>367</volume><fpage>1937</fpage><lpage>1946</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16765763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Anselmi1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anselmi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Moreira</surname><given-names>J-M</given-names></name><name><surname>Caicedo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Guderian</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tognoni</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Community participation eliminates yaws in Ecuador.</article-title><source>Trop Med Int Health</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>634</fpage><lpage>638</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12828546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Scolnik1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scolnik</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Aronson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lovinsky</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Toledano</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Glazier</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Efficacy of a targeted, oral penicillin&#x02013;based yaws control program among children living in rural South America.</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>1232</fpage><lpage>1238</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12746767</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Hopkins1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hopkins</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1976</year><article-title>After smallpox eradication: Yaws?</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>860</fpage><lpage>865</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1034444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-International1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>International Task Force for Disease Eradication</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Summary of the eleventh meeting of the ITFDE (II).</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cartercenter.org/documents/itfde_summaryoct07.pdf">http://www.cartercenter.org/documents/itfde_summaryoct07.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 1 August 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-World2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Informal consultation on yaws.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/neglected_diseases/diseases/ic24_26_jan2007.pdf">http://www.who.int/neglected_diseases/diseases/ic24_26_jan2007.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 1 August 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Levrero1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levrero</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Gatti</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gautier-Hion</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Menard</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Yaws disease in a wild gorilla population and its impact on the reproductive status of males.</article-title><source>Am J Phys Anthropol</source><volume>132</volume><fpage>568</fpage><lpage>575</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17274014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Wallis1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wallis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rick</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Primate conservation: The prevention of disease transmission.</article-title><source>Int J Primatol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>803</fpage><lpage>826</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-World3"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>Yaws eradication in the South-East Asia region.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.searo.who.int/LinkFiles/Yaws_yaws.pdf">http://www.searo.who.int/LinkFiles/Yaws_yaws.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 1 August 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Bora1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bora</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dhariwal</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lal</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Yaws and its eradication in India&#x02014;A brief review.</article-title><source>J Commun Dis</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16637394</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Lahariya1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lahariya</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pradhan</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Can Southeast Asia eradicate yaws by 2010? Some lessons from the Yaws Eradication Programme of India.</article-title><source>Natl Med J India</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>86</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17802987</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000275-Aylward1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aylward</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Birmingham</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Eradicating pathogens. The human history.</article-title><source>BMJ</source><volume>331</volume><fpage>1261</fpage><lpage>1264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16308391</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p>The author received a commissioning fee from <italic>PLoS Neglected Tropical Diseases</italic> for writing this article.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>